; EzyMap Scalp Mastery V2.2 BTC - EzyMap_V2_2_BTCUSD_STAGE0_BASELINE.set
; STAGE 0 - CONTROL. Every input V2.2 BTC introduces, pinned to the value
; that reproduces V2.1b EXACTLY. This is the A/B control arm: run it on
; XAUUSD against a V2.1b binary and the two must be indistinguishable.
;
; POLARITY: back to the pre-V2.1b convention. V2.1b was the odd stage out -
; both of ITS inputs defaulted to the NEW behaviour, so its baseline file was
; the all-TRUE rollback. V2.2 BTC returns to the normal rule: every new input
; DEFAULTS to reproducing the base, so this file is byte-identical to the
; compiled-in defaults and exists only so the control arm is explicit in the
; tester rather than implied. It does NOT roll anything back.
;
; ONLY FOUR INPUTS ARE LISTED because V2.2 BTC only added four. S01
; (NearGoldRoundNumber symbol awareness) and S02 (live cent protection parity
; gate widened to BTC) are UNCONDITIONAL CODE FIXES with no input and no
; rollback switch. They are safe to ship without one because both are no-ops
; on gold BY CONSTRUCTION, not by configuration:
;
;   S01 - for any gold symbol the new majorStep/minorStep resolve to the
;         literals 10.0 and 5.0 that the old code had hardcoded. Same
;         arithmetic, same result. (They also resolve to 10.0/5.0 for ANY
;         symbol quoted below ~1000, because the fallback branch is
;         MathMax(price*0.01,10.0).)
;   S02 - the gate widened from IsGold() to IsGold()||IsBTC(). Widening a
;         disjunction cannot make a previously-true case false, so no symbol
;         that engaged the feature before can stop engaging it now.
;
; S04 changes printed TEXT only, never a value, a threshold or a branch.
;
; Load this ON TOP of your V2.1b working set - every other input keeps its
; current value.
;
; Confirm from the OnInit log that you loaded it. This file must produce:
;   V2.2 BTC S3 LEVEL MIN-DISTANCE FLOORS | H4=70.0 pips ... | D1=120.0 pips
;   ... | W1=200.0 pips ... | H1=70.0 pips ...
;   ... | defaults 70/120/200/70 reproduce V2.1b exactly
;
InpH4LevelMinDistancePips=70.0
InpD1LevelMinDistancePips=120.0
InpW1LevelMinDistancePips=200.0
InpH1LevelMinDistancePips=70.0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; S06 (added after S01-S05) - InpForceMinimumBaseSizing
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; S06 breaks the "four inputs" count above: it added a FIFTH, and it is the
; one V2.2 BTC input that does NOT default to reproducing the base. It
; DEFAULTS TO TRUE - a deliberate polarity exception, requested explicitly -
; so this control file must pin it FALSE to keep this arm a true V2.1b
; reproduction.
;
; What it does: floors the NOMINAL lot-sizing target so LotSizingCapitalUnits()
; never reports less than InpBaseEquity, i.e. an account below 100 deposit
; units still sizes as if it had 100. It reaches NO risk or margin
; calculation - CapSetupVolumeForCentSafety() and
; CapVolumeForStandardRiskGuard() read ACCOUNT_EQUITY and
; OrderCalcProfit/OrderCalcMargin directly and still have the final word.
;
; At 100 deposit units or above the floored and unfloored formulas are
; arithmetically IDENTICAL, so at any normal tester deposit this arm and the
; default arm produce the same lots. Seeing no difference is expected.
;
; S06's other half - the DEPLOYMENT GATE BREAKDOWN log line - is pure
; instrumentation with no input and no rollback switch. It prints in both
; arms and changes no behaviour, so it does not compromise this control.
InpForceMinimumBaseSizing=false
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; S07 (added after S06) - InpAutoCalibrateSpreadCap
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Same polarity exception as S06, for the same reason: this is the input that
; makes SpreadAllowed() measure the real spread instead of comparing against
; the static InpMaxSpreadPoints. It DEFAULTS TO TRUE in this file (three
; static-cap guesses failed on BTCUSD.sc); pin it FALSE here so this control
; arm enforces the plain static cap exactly as V2.1b/gold always have.
InpAutoCalibrateSpreadCap=false
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; S08 (added after S07) - InpUseATRGeometry / InpATRStopCeilingPips
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Same polarity exception again: InpUseATRGeometry DEFAULTS TO TRUE in this
; file (a flat 21-pip = $21 stop on BTC proved far too tight - 12% win rate
; on a real test run), with InpATRStopCeilingPips raised 35 -> 500 so that
; ceiling cannot silently clamp the ATR-derived stop back down to a
; gold-sized figure. Pin both back to their pre-S08 values here so this
; control arm runs the plain fixed-pip geometry exactly as V2.1b/gold always
; have.
InpUseATRGeometry=false
InpATRStopCeilingPips=35.0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; S09 (added after S08) - InpZeroConfFallbackMinConfluences
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Same polarity exception again: this file's low-exposure fallback assigns
; InpZeroConfFallbackMinConfluences (DEFAULT 2 here) instead of a hardcoded
; 0 to setups admitted while flat/near-flat, which routes them through the
; normal deployment quality gate instead of the FORCE-PASS bypass. Pin it
; back to 0 here so this control arm reproduces the exact pre-S09 "any touch
; while flat" behaviour, unchanged since V3.094/V3.102.
InpZeroConfFallbackMinConfluences=0
